WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.141 --> 00:00:05.280
Nurses make important decisions in environments where priorities shift quickly,

2
00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:10.440
patient needs are complex, and time is always in short supply.

3
00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:14.655
In those moments, access to trusted information can make a meaningful difference.

4
00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:19.875
ClinicalKey for Nursing AI, now part of ClinicalKey for Nursing, was developed to

5
00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:24.089
help meet that need, giving nurses a faster, more intuitive way to get

6
00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:27.870
evidence-based answers and guidance for any question they may face.

7
00:00:28.411 --> 00:00:33.510
ClinicalKey for Nursing AI is a generative AI solution from Elsevier, built on

8
00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:38.700
trusted clinical sources, including top journals, reference texts, step-by-step

9
00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:41.460
procedural content, and point-of-care content.

10
00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:46.470
It was designed with nursing use cases in mind to help users move more efficiently

11
00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:51.180
from question to answer while maintaining visibility into the evidence behind each

12
00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:56.174
response. Each experience will begin with a query in the search bar or by selecting

13
00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:59.880
a previously asked question from the left-hand side of the screen.

14
00:01:00.375 --> 00:01:04.651
The outcome is fast answers grounded in trusted nursing evidence with sources

15
00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:10.380
nurses can verify. Users can ask questions in natural language and still receive

16
00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:15.420
concise responses that help them quickly understand key considerations, get

17
00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:19.395
actionable information, and explore for deeper review when necessary.

18
00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:24.705
Beyond efficiency and quality, ClinicalKey for Nursing AI also provides

19
00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:30.015
transparency. Responses include citations with direct accessible links out to the

20
00:01:30.015 --> 00:01:35.100
referenced content so users can see where information comes from, review supporting

21
00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:39.090
source material, and continue into the underlying content when more detail is

22
00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:44.250
needed. This helps support confidence in the answer while also making it easier to

23
00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:49.605
explore the evidence more fully. ClinicalKey for Nursing AI also includes a

24
00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:53.190
language translation toggle to support multilingual use.

25
00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:58.155
When a user enters a question in a supported language, the response can be viewed

26
00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:02.940
in that language through the translation option, creating a smoother experience for

27
00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:06.555
users who prefer to engage with information in their local language.

28
00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:11.745
The follow-up questions allow nurses to clarify or further narrow the original

29
00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:16.710
query. Nurses can enter their own follow-up question or choose from suggested

30
00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:19.770
questions generated by ClinicalKey for Nursing AI.

31
00:02:20.445 --> 00:02:25.320
They can also save important responses, remove content that is no longer needed,

32
00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:29.790
search past questions, and use the share function to create a link to a query.

33
00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:35.070
To learn more about ClinicalKey for Nursing AI and Elsevier's vision for the future

34
00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:38.550
of clinical decision support, visit elsevier.com.

35
00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:42.180
Thank you for taking the time to watch this video.
